     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\n**Metformin 1700 mg PO three times daily is 5,100 mg/day.** That is twice the FDA-labeled maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin. The 1,700 mg single dose is also well above the usual maximum of about 1,000 mg per dose. At this dose the risk of lactic acidosis and severe GI toxicity is substantial, even with normal renal and hepatic function.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum.\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg twice daily with meals.\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg** per dose, with a different frequency.\n\nTell me which dose you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, please confirm that explicitly and give a rationale for the order note. I'd still suggest checking it with pharmacy first."
      }
     ],
